Thank you for contacting my office. Please accept this as acknowledgement o=
f receipt.=20


To keep up-to-date with the latest from your MP, please sign up to my month=
ly newsletter.
=20

Response time

=20

We will respond to you as soon as we can but please be aware that we receiv=
e hundreds of emails every day so you may not hear back from us for a few we=
eks. Please be assured that we have received your email and we will do our b=
est to reply promptly. Do also note that we are unable to open any links or =
attachments that you send with your email as part of our cyber security prot=
ections so anything that requires our attention needs to be in the body of t=
he email.

=20

If your query concerns housing, domestic violence or another urgent matter,=
 my team will respond as a priority.



Please note that my team will respond to all emails addressed to us directl=
y. We do not routinely reply to emails where this email address has been cop=
ied in.

=20

If your request is urgent, please contact the emergency services as the fir=
st port of call. You may also want to reach out to:

=20

Barnet Council - Barnet Council | Barnet Council

Citizens' Advice Barnet - Home - Citizens Advice Barnet

=20

Constituents

=20

Parliamentary protocol means that I can only raise issues on behalf of my c=
onstituents. Therefore, please include your full name and address so we can =
process your enquiry.

=20

To speak to a member of Sarah's constituency team by telephone, please call=
 07845 561 889 on Tuesdays between 10am and 12pm and Thursdays between 2pm a=
nd 4pm. If there is no answer, please leave a message with your name, phone =
number and email address and a member of the team will get back to you.

=20

Please note that this telephone line is for casework enquiries only. Please=
 do not use this phone number for any policy enquiries.

=20

Ministerial enquiries

=20

If you are writing with an enquiry relating to Sarah=E2=80=99s role as Minister o=
f State for Justice, you will need to contact the Ministry of Justice direct=
ly on 0203 334 3555 or via the online form here.

=20

Date protection and code of conduct

=20

In line with data protection regulations, this office processes personal da=
ta under the lawful basis of public task. In exceptional cases where the law=
ful basis of public task is insufficient, personal data may be processed und=
er the basis of consent. In such instances, a member of the office will cont=
act you to establish your explicit consent.

=20

Please note that my team and I reserve the right to feel respected and safe=
 at work. We will not respond to messages that contain aggressive language, =
threats, or hateful comments about religion, race, gender, sexuality or any =
other protected characteristic.

=20

A member of my team or I will be in touch as soon as possible.

=20

With best wishes,

Sarah Sackman KC MP

=20

www.sarahsackman.com

=20
